    "knowledge_point": "Computing the One-Sided Limits of a Piecewise Function when the Limits Do Not Coincide",
    "problem": "Find the left-sided limit at $x=0$ for the function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x & \\text{ for }\\,-\\frac{\\pi }{2}<x\\le 0 \\\\ {log}_{2}⁡x & \\text{ for }\\,x>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "worked_solution": "Approaching from the left, we have $x<0,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
